/-!
# The echelon basis of `S₂`: canonical states, grades and triangularity at the pivots

Kernel-checked facts about the data of `S2Data.lean` (generated by
`lean/tools/lattice_export/gen_s2.py`), assembled from the per-vector checks of
`S2PivotsA`–`F` (states) and `S2Tri00`–`32` (pivots): all states of `u` and of the `r_k` are
canonical (sorted code lists) and the `r_k` have grade two (`s2basis_states`); `r_k` has
coefficient `1` at its pivot (`s2piv_diag`) and `0` at the pivots of all earlier `r_j`
(`j < k`, `s2piv_low`), which makes the `r_k` linearly independent (`S2Link.lean`).  (The
docstrings of the pieces call this file `S2Pivots.lean`, its name in the generated drafts.)
-/


